      "math_academy_id": "e-3245",
      "problem": "In the right triangle $\\triangle ABC,$ the angle $\\angle A$ is a right angle, and the side lengths are $AB=2,$ $AC=\\sqrt{5},$ and $BC=3.$ Find $\\tan B.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's illustrate the given triangle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244094/assets/4e4e2005e31716a09953aed9054cc5796ee915d41d5a9020042984b348e3b743.png)\n\nThe tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to $\\angle B,$ the opposite side is $\\overline{AC},$ and the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\tan{B} &= \\dfrac{AC}{AB} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\n\t}\n$$",
